In a #large bowl{}, combine @eggnog{2%cups}, @heavy cream{1%cup}, @sugar{3/4%cup}, @vanilla extract{1%tsp}, @nutmeg{1%tsp}, @cinnamon{1/2%tsp}, and @salt{1/4%tsp}.

Whisk for ~{2-3%minutes}, until the sugar is dissolved into the mixture. You should not feel any grit if you rub the mixture together between two fingers.

If mixture is not cold, put it in the fridge for ~{30%minutes} first.

Add the mixture to the bowl of your ice cream machine. Churn according to your manufacturer's instructions (mine took about 25-30 minutes), until it is thick and the consistency of soft-serve ice cream.

Freeze for at least 4 hours, or until solid.